                "text": "**Analyzing Line-Dot Relationships**\n\nI'm now focusing on the relationship between lines and dots, specifically their positions. I've broken down the first example to understand how line centers relate to dot positions. I've realized that the dot color is 8, and it's located at the center of the line. I'm moving toward creating a rule about the connections.\n\n\n**Investigating Dot-Line Connections**\n\nI've discovered a pattern: a perpendicular line segment, length 3, of the dot's color, is placed centered at the midpoint of the line. The original dot seems to be removed. I've tested this on multiple examples, confirming this rule. I'm now looking at Example 3, to see if it holds across different color combinations.\n\n\n",
